# Multitrack, stopped: a black key previews its track's note on that track's own channel. Press a second row
# before the first is let go, and the first note ends on its own channel (it used to be let go on the new
# track's, and hang on the first's).
wait 300
press GLO
tap SEQ
release GLO
spin K4 3
tap HOME
expect mode 3
# tracks 1, 2 and 3 (b1, b2, b3) each moved off the default channel (the spins land them on 12, 14 and 16)
tapkey b1
press GLO
tap SEQ
tap SEQ
release GLO
expect menu 10
spin K1 2
tap HOME
tapkey b2
press GLO
tap SEQ
tap SEQ
release GLO
spin K1 4
tap HOME
tapkey b3
press GLO
tap SEQ
tap SEQ
release GLO
spin K1 6
tap HOME
wait 300
expect hanging 0
expect playing 0
# one row at a time
key b1 down
wait 100
expect hanging 1
key b1 up
wait 100
expect hanging 0
# the next row pressed while the first is held: the first ends, the second sounds
key b1 down
wait 100
key b2 down
wait 100
expect hanging 1
key b1 up
wait 50
expect hanging 1
key b2 up
wait 100
expect hanging 0
# three rows rolled over each other
key b1 down
wait 60
key b2 down
wait 60
key b3 down
wait 60
key b1 up
key b2 up
key b3 up
wait 200
expect hanging 0
expect chnotes12 >0
expect chnotes14 >0
expect chnotes16 >0
